<title>USA: Richmond Fed regional survey for June.</title>
<headline>Richmond Fed regional survey for June.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federal Reserve Bank of Richmond indexes monitoring manufacturing and service-sector activity.</p>
<p> MANUFACTURING SURVEY    June    May</p>
<p>  Shipments		    15     21</p>
<p>  New Orders		   11     16</p>
<p>  Backlog Orders	     -6     -6</p>
<p>  Number of Employees	 7     11</p>
<p>  Average Workweek	    0	4</p>
<p>  Prices Received	  0.85  -0.37</p>
<p>  Prices Paid		1.30   0.61</p>
<p> SERVICES SURVEY	   June    May</p>
<p>  Service Revenues	   33     26</p>
<p>  Number of Employees	10     19</p>
<p>  Service Wage		 25     26</p>
<p>  Retail Revenues	    21     14</p>
<p>  Retail Employees	    9	4</p>
<p>  Retail Wage		  21     25</p>
<p>  Shopper Traffic	    -5     19</p>
<p>Note -- Each index equals the percentage of responding firms reporting increases minus the percentage reporting decreases. Prices received and prices paid are in response to the question &quot;What do you believe was the percentage price change in your industry on an annualized basis?&quot;</p>
<p>Results of the June manufacturing survey are based on responses from 75 of 178 firms queried. Results of the June service-sector survey are based on responses from 61 of 121 firms.</p>
</text>
